# Figma MCP builds the site

Every new website arrives as a Figma file. Copy briefs do not pick layout, section order, card counts, image side, or palette.

Build in this order. Do not compose full pages before tokens and atoms match Figma.

1. **Design system** — `src/brand.ts` (colors, fonts, radius). See the `tokens` rule.
2. **Atoms** — restyle `Button`, `Headline`, `Form`, cards in `src/components/ui/` to match Figma. No per-page forks.
3. **Sections** — one widget per pattern (`FAQs`, `Hero2`, `CTABanner`, …). Restyle the existing file; do not add `HomeFAQ`.
4. **Pages** — `src/pages/[route]/index.astro` only composes those widgets.

## Source of truth

1. Authenticate the Figma MCP server if tools are unavailable (`mcp_auth`).
2. Extract tokens first (see the `tokens` rule) into `src/brand.ts`. Copy desktop **and** mobile type from Figma when both exist. Fill `src/config/site.ts` + `contact.ts`.
3. Restyle atoms (`Button`, `Headline`, inputs, cards) until they match Figma components.
4. Restyle or add **one** section widget per repeating pattern. Register new widgets (see `components` rule).
5. Walk each page frame top to bottom: screenshot + structure. Compose the page from those widgets (backgrounds, type, spacing, image side, item counts from Figma).
6. After page work, run `npm run build` and fix errors before finishing.

## Always-on stack

Keep Sanity, Resend/forms (`/contact`), GTM, Search Console, JSON-LD, reviews, blog, and legal routes. Fill client IDs in `src/config/site.ts`, `src/config/contact.ts`, and `.env` — do not delete the wiring. See `ONBOARDING.md`.

## Do not

- Invent layout from a content doc, outline, or sitemap
- Apply a canned section color cycle (white → grey → dark, or any other)
- Auto-flip split images, ban 5-card grids, or force icon-point bands from item counts
- Implement a page before tokens are in `src/brand.ts` when the Figma file has a distinct palette/type
- Skip atoms / dump unique markup into a page file
- Fork a section per route (`HomeFAQ`, `AboutHero`, `ServicesCTA`)
